# docs/family-roster.txt is a generated, sorted list of every document behind a
# collapsed-family row in the documentation map. Every branch that adds a skill,
# an SOP, or a reference inserts a line into it, and two insertions into the same
# gap conflict even when the two names are not adjacent -- git has no unchanged
# context line between them to anchor on. Several of the governance pull requests
# in flight land in one such gap, so without this the roster would merely inherit
# the conflict the map was fixed to stop having.
#
# Git's built-in union driver keeps the lines from both sides, needs no per-clone
# config, and cannot lose an insertion. Where it produces the wrong content --
# out of sort order, or a line one side deliberately deleted -- the roster no
# longer matches its generator, `make docs-check` fails on it, and
# `make docs-generate` writes the correct file. That is the same recovery the
# roster's own header describes, so the deletion guard survives the union merge.
docs/family-roster.txt merge=union
